    "formulaExplanation": "Uses a human-life-value approach: income multiplied by the chosen replacement period, plus liabilities and dependant goals, less existing life cover.",
    "example": "Rs 12 lakh annual income for 15 years, Rs 30 lakh of liabilities and Rs 40 lakh of goals produces a Rs 2.5 crore need before existing cover.",
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "Is the calculated amount a policy recommendation?",
        "answer": "No. It is an educational cover-gap estimate; affordability, health, insurer underwriting and policy terms also matter."
      },
      {
        "question": "Should employer life insurance count as existing cover?",
        "answer": "You may include it, but remember that employer cover can end when you change or leave a job."
